# Spreading from the landing site to the whole planet.
#
# `play.4x` walks the first five steps of the loop and stops with territory 1 working
# every node and territory 2 founded. This continues to steps 6, 7 and 8: reach the rest
# of the planet, build a Yard where one can be built, produce an Ark, and launch it.
#
# The adjacency is the smallest Goldberg solid's, so territory 1 touches 2 to 6, and
# 7 to 12 are reached through them:
#
#   1: 2 3 4 5 6      5: 1 3 6 9 12     9: 3 5 7 11 12
#   2: 1 3 4 7 8      6: 1 4 5 10 12   10: 4 6 8 11 12
#   3: 1 2 5 7 9      7: 2 3 8 9 11    11: 7 8 9 10 12
#   4: 1 2 6 8 10     8: 2 4 7 10 11   12: 5 6 9 10 11
#
# Territory 1 makes twelve metal and twelve energy a turn against a pioneer's eight and
# six, so it can send one out every turn once it is working every node.

# Turn 7. The landing site feeds itself, then sends the next pioneer to territory 3.
work 3 extractor 1 food
work 3 extractor 1 metal
work 3 extractor 1 energy
work 1 extractor 2 food
produce pioneer 1
end turn

# Turn 8. The pioneer crosses to territory 3 and founds it. The landing site is at eleven
# citizens rather than twelve from here on: a pioneer waiting to leave eats one food a
# turn, so the population settles one below the ceiling for as long as one is standing
# there. Nine of the eleven hands work the nine extractors; the other two are spare.
move pioneer 3
work 1 extractor 3 food
work 3 extractor 1 food
work 3 extractor 1 metal
work 3 extractor 1 energy
work 1 extractor 2 food
produce pioneer 1
end turn

# Turn 9. Territory 2 has grown, so it opens its second food node while territory 3 feeds
# itself. The next pioneer goes to 4.
move pioneer 4
work 1 extractor 4 food
work 1 extractor 3 food
build extractor 2 food
work 2 extractor 2 food
work 3 extractor 1 food
work 3 extractor 1 metal
work 3 extractor 1 energy
produce pioneer 1
end turn
